{"availability":"available","full":"Jareltis/braille-art-generator","name":"braille-art-generator","description":"Turn any picture into art made of Unicode braille dots — in the browser, offline, no dependencies. Dithering, XDoG contours, colour, and a suggest button that scores its own output.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-12-07T20:29:43Z","updated":"2026-09-05T19:21:48Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jareltis.github.io/braille-art-generator/","topics":["ascii-art","braille","canvas","dithering","halftone","image-to-text","javascript","no-dependencies","pwa","unicode"],"demo":"https://jareltis.github.io/braille-art-generator/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:31:20.818Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T19:31:20.818Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T19:31:20.818Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:44:56.732Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T19:31:20.818Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Turns an image into text made of Unicode braille glyphs (U+2800…U+28FF). Each glyph encodes a 2×4 block of pixels, so it carries four times the detail of ordinary ASCII art.","It runs entirely in the browser: the image is never uploaded, and the server only ever hands out static files.","Generators like to state that Discord is \"about 30 characters\" and Twitch \"about 20\". Those numbers look authoritative and are worth nothing: the width moves with the device, the window, the zoom, the client's own font size setting and whether the art sits in a code block."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jareltis/braille-art-generator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e28458898fcb2d339445a267874d170c8162e9bfd45593e95e6edb8344c8ab92","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:56.933Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:56.933Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Turns an image into text made of Unicod